"\"The captain who remained does not tell his dead friend the truth. No error.\"",
"The machine being right does not make it the wrong choice. Captain Roran is carrying that as he walks. That is walking, too.",
"Printout: the lantern",
"\"The fisherman cannot put out the lantern.\" But he did. Because you were beside him.",
"'Error.' It seems the machine cannot reckon with someone standing at your side.",
"\"The fisherman cannot put out the lantern. No error.\" But there is one more line after it.",
"'On the day the sea has fully thawed, two hands put it out.' Two hands. I hear you promised. Let the machine be right about that one.",
"Printout: the last line",
"The last line is about the glove. 'What guides that hand is the glove. No error.'",
"But under it, a line was half printed and stopped. 'What removes the glove is' and no further. The paper ends there. Because the machine fell.",
"…We cut it off. So we could not hear the answer. Or perhaps it could not print what has not been decided yet.",
"The answer to the King of Frost",
"You said, 'I am afraid, so I fight beside the one who will write my name.' At the door of the burial chamber.",
"My hand shook as I wrote that down. Because the one who writes the names is me. I did not know then how great a thing that was.",
"When I wrote a name on my palm in the Nether, I remembered those words. I was afraid. I wrote anyway. Because someone was fighting beside me.",
"You said, 'I am not afraid. I walk because there is an end.' At the door of the burial chamber.",
"The king was quiet for a long while after hearing that. To a man who had been afraid for a thousand years because there was no end, you said you walk because there is one.",
"The Elder heard it too, from the doorframe. The man who sold a life that does not end. …I think those words hurt the Elder most of all.",
"The broken line of the printout",
"The last line of the Harbinger's printout. The one that broke off at 'What removes the glove is.'",
"I thought words like 'the surveyors' or 'a blade' would follow. They did not. The Elder took off the glove. Himself. Because he promised.",
"It is not that the machine failed to print it. It could not. It seems what a person does of their own will does not enter the reckoning.",
"The name that was spoken",
"You spoke the name to him. Once only, slowly. The Elder repeated it. Only with his lips. Without a sound.",
"Then he said, 'That is enough.' He did not grasp it again. He has become someone who can hear it and still let go. It took a thousand years.",
"The name that was not spoken",
"You told him to read it himself on the day he is able to let go. The Elder nodded. He said thank you.",
"The Chronicle lies open in the archive. At that page. The Elder's door is not locked. I don't know when he will come up. There is no hurry.",
"Captain Roran",
"Whenever anyone leaves the village, the Captain counts heads. Once going out, once coming back. At first I thought he was just strict.",
"He checks a newcomer's bootlaces three times. Mine too. I wrote that in the margin of the Chronicle as 'nagging'… I think I should erase it. He had his reasons.",
"The Elder",
"The Elder never comes to the restaurant. He says he cannot take hot things. He even lets his tea go cold before drinking it.",
"And the gloves. He wore them when he taught me my letters, even in high summer. When I was little I thought all grown-ups did.",
"An old sea song has this verse: 'We had a ship. The sister who went out to meet them did not return.' The Chronicle has not one line about that sister.",
"You're here. …Can't call you apprentice any more. I still count heads. One.",
