"Put that spear away. …No, never mind. Keep hold of it. Standing next to it, I can see their faces clearly. Strange thing.",
"The leg? Twenty years old. The day before rain, I know before the clouds do.",
"The rusted knight, the ice giant, the mason on the mountaintop, the priest of the sun. The places my expedition passed twenty years ago.",
"Back then I only thought they were monsters. It never crossed my mind to read what was written on the walls.",
"This time we read before we go. Knowing how your opponent lives before the fight is a captain's job.",
"Cornelia, captain of the ghost ship. A ship that stopped in the ice fifteen years ago with three hundred aboard.",
"No one in this village curses that captain. The fishing boats that went out to save the ship never came back either.",
"I know nothing about fire or names. I only know the people I know.",
"But this I know. For twenty years their faces have been fading. What Thomas's nose looked like, which eye Lia winked with. The fading was what frightened me most.",
"Under that spear's dusk light, it comes back. All of it. Thomas had a crooked nose. Lia, the left eye. …I don't know if this is good. Some things you have to forget to go on living.",
"Show it to the archivist. That girl will know what it ought to be used for.",
"The band that cleared the way",
"The Ashen Band had made camp on the road to the Nether. I thought we'd fight. They cleared the way. Stood aside, left and right.",
"The one in front said, 'The one who owes is the one who remembers.' Kass. The captain you let go at the storehouse.",
"He said he saw the archivist being dragged off. Told us which way they went, too. …I was taught that an enemy you let go stabs you in the back. Twenty years of learning it wrong.",
